.\" Manpage for termshot.
.\" Contact the project maintainers to correct errors or typos.
.TH TERMSHOT 1 "2026-08-25" "termshot 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
termshot \- capture terminal screenshots with full ANSI rendering
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B termshot
.RI [ GLOBAL\ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.br
.B termshot exec
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I command ...
.br
.B termshot render
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I input
.br
.B termshot compose
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I image1 image2 ...
.br
.B termshot mcp
.br
.B termshot themes
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B termshot
runs a command in a pseudo\-terminal (PTY), captures its output including all
ANSI escape sequences (colors, bold, cursor movement), and renders a PNG that
looks like a real terminal window. It can decorate the output with window
chrome (GNOME, macOS, or report styles), apply color themes, and redact known
secret formats from the rendered image on request.
.PP
Commands run through your shell as a login and interactive shell
.RI ( $SHELL " \-l \-i" ),
so a capture inherits the environment you normally work in: profile files are
sourced, and your prompt (PS1), aliases, shell functions,
.BR PATH ,
and exports all apply. Aliases apply too: if
.B cat
is aliased to
.BR bat / batcat ,
.B termshot exec \(aqcat file\(aq
captures bat\(aqs output. Bypass an alias the way you would interactively, with
.BR "command cat" ,
.BR \(rscat ,
or
.BR \-\-no\-prompt ,
which runs the command non\-interactively
.RI ( $SHELL " \-c" )
where aliases are not defined and no prompt is drawn. The shell itself can be
changed with the
.B shell
config key or
.BR TERMSHOT_SHELL .
.PP
The screen is reset before the command runs, so shell startup banners stay out
of the image and every capture shows exactly one prompt: the one in front of
the command. The trailing prompt the shell draws afterwards is removed as well,
including the upper lines of a multi\-line PS1.
.PP
The same binary doubles as a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server
.RB ( termshot\ mcp ),
exposing the
.BR execute_and_screenshot ,
.BR render_ansi ,
.BR redact_screenshot ,
and
.B compose_screenshots
tools so an AI agent can capture, inspect, redact, and combine screenshots
programmatically.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
These options are accepted before or after any subcommand.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Path to the configuration file. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/termshot/config.toml .
.TP
.BI \-\-rules\-path " DIR"
Additional directory of redaction rule files
.RI ( .toml
plus Kingfisher
.IR .yaml )
loaded on top of the built\-in rules, the config rules, and the default user
rules directory
.IR ~/.config/termshot/rules/ .
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS exec
Execute a command and save a terminal screenshot.
.PP
.B termshot exec
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I command ...
.PP
Everything after the options is treated as the command to run. Multiple
arguments are each executed on their own line, each with its own PS1 prompt.
.TP
.BI \-c, \-\-cols " N"
Terminal width in columns, 1\-500 (default: 120).
.TP
.BI \-r, \-\-rows " N"
Terminal viewport height in rows, 1\-500 (default: 40). This is the terminal the
command runs in, not a limit on what the screenshot shows: output that scrolls
off the top is retained and rendered. See
.B VIEWPORT AND RETAINED OUTPUT
below.
.TP
.BI \-\-head\-lines " N"
Show only the first N lines of the output \- the first N lines the command
printed, however much it went on to print afterwards. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-tail\-lines .
.TP
.BI \-\-tail\-lines " N"
Show only the last N lines of the output, like
.BR "tail \-n" .
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-head\-lines .
.TP
.BI \-t, \-\-timeout " SECS"
Maximum time to wait for the command to finish (default: 30).
.TP
.BI \-\-chrome " PRESET"
Window chrome preset: one of
.BR none ,
.BR minimal ,
.BR gnome ,
.BR macos ,
.BR report .
.TP
.BI \-\-font " PATH"
Path to a regular font file, overriding the embedded JetBrains Mono.
.TP
.BI \-\-font\-bold " PATH"
Path to a bold font file (uses a real bold face instead of faux bold).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-prompt
Run the command non\-interactively via
.RI $SHELL " \-c" ,
hiding the shell prompt (PS1). Startup files are not sourced, so aliases and
shell functions are not available.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
Theme name (e.g.
.BR dark ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR tokyo\-night ).
.TP
.BI \-\-title " TITLE"
Optional chrome title bar text.
.TP
.B \-\-timestamp
Add a UTC timestamp watermark below the terminal content.
.TP
.BI \-o, \-\-output " PATH"
Output file path. When omitted, a descriptively named file is auto\-generated
in the output directory (see
.BR "OUTPUT AND NAMING" ).
.TP
.B \-\-redact
Redact sensitive data (IPs, keys, tokens, ...) from this screenshot.
.TP
.BI \-\-redact\-rules " RULES"
Comma\-separated list of redaction rule names to apply (default: all enabled
rules). Implies
.BR \-\-redact .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-redact
Force redaction off even when auto\-redaction is enabled in the config.
.TP
.B \-\-redact\-text
Also redact the returned plain text. By default only the PNG is redacted and
the text keeps the original (unredacted) content.
.TP
.B \-\-plain\-text
Return plain text with ANSI color codes stripped. By default the original
output is returned with colors preserved.
.TP
.BI \-\-auto\-crop " BOOL"
Trim the image width to the rightmost content instead of using the full
terminal width, keeping the same padding on the right as on the left
(default: true).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-description
Do not embed the terminal text in the PNG
.B Description
metadata. By default the text (redacted, when redaction ran) is embedded as a
UTF\-8
.B iTXt
chunk so screen readers can read the screenshot.
.TP
.B \-\-rounded, \-\-no\-rounded
Draw soft rounded corners (default) or square corners. With chrome the window
frame is rounded; without chrome the terminal image itself gets rounded corners
on a transparent background.
.SS render
Render raw ANSI terminal output to a PNG screenshot, without executing
anything.
.PP
.B termshot render
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I input
.PP
.I input
is a file containing raw ANSI output, or
.B \-
to read from standard input (for example
.BR "cmd \-\-color=always | termshot render \-" ).
.TP
.BI \-c, \-\-cols " N"
Terminal width in columns, 1\-500 (default: 120).
.TP
.BI \-r, \-\-rows " N"
Terminal viewport height in rows, 1\-500 (default: 40). A file taller than the
viewport is rendered whole, not clipped to its last screenful.
.TP
.BI \-\-head\-lines " N"
Render only the first N lines. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-tail\-lines .
.TP
.BI \-\-tail\-lines " N"
Render only the last N lines. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-head\-lines .
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
Theme name.
.TP
.BI \-\-chrome " PRESET"
Window chrome preset:
.BR none ,
.BR minimal ,
.BR gnome ,
.BR macos ,
.BR report .
.TP
.BI \-\-title " TITLE"
Optional chrome title.
.TP
.B \-\-timestamp
Add a UTC timestamp watermark below the terminal content.
.TP
.BI \-o, \-\-output " PATH"
Output file path.
.TP
.B \-\-plain\-text
Return plain text with ANSI color codes stripped.
.TP
.B \-\-redact
Redact sensitive data from this render. The same
.B [redaction]
policy as
.B exec
applies.
.TP
.BI \-\-redact\-rules " RULES"
Comma\-separated list of redaction rule names to apply. Implies
.BR \-\-redact .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-redact
Force redaction off even when auto\-redaction is enabled in the config.
.TP
.B \-\-redact\-text
Also redact the returned plain text.
.TP
.BI \-\-auto\-crop " BOOL"
Trim the image width to the rightmost content instead of using the full
terminal width, keeping the same padding on the right as on the left
(default: true).
.TP
.B \-\-rounded, \-\-no\-rounded
Draw soft rounded corners (default) or square corners.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-description
Do not embed the terminal text in the PNG
.B Description
metadata.
.SS compose
Compose two or more screenshots side by side or stacked into one image.
.PP
.B termshot compose
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I image1 image2 ...
.PP
At least two input PNGs are required; they are placed in the order given and
stretched to a common height (horizontal) or width (vertical). When
.B embed_description
is enabled, the panes\(aq
.B Description
metadata is read back and joined (separated by
.RB ` "--- Pane N ---" `
markers) into the composed image\(aqs own
.B Description
chunk.
.TP
.BI \-\-layout " LAYOUT"
.B horizontal
(side by side) or
.B vertical
(stacked). Default:
.BR vertical .
.TP
.BI \-\-divider " PIXELS"
Divider thickness in pixels between adjacent panes, drawn as a thin solid line
like a tmux split (default: 2; use 0 for none). Panes are padded, never
rescaled, to a common height (horizontal) or width (vertical), so their text
stays pixel\-exact.
.TP
.BI \-\-chrome " PRESET"
Wrap the composed result in a single outer window frame:
.BR none ,
.BR minimal ,
.BR gnome ,
.BR macos ,
.BR report .
Inputs should be raw (chrome\-less) screenshots so only this outer frame is
drawn.
.TP
.BI \-\-title " TITLE"
Optional title for the outer chrome frame (only used with
.BR \-\-chrome ).
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
Theme name whose background color fills the canvas.
.TP
.BI \-o, \-\-output " PATH"
Output file path. When omitted, a file is auto\-generated in the output
directory.
.SS mcp
Start the MCP server on stdio. Exposes the
.BR execute_and_screenshot ,
.BR render_ansi ,
.BR redact_screenshot ,
and
.B compose_screenshots
tools. Each screenshot\(aqs raw output and render metadata are kept in memory
for the lifetime of the process so
.B redact_screenshot
can re\-render it; records are lost on restart and are not created by the CLI.
.SS themes
List available themes. Each theme is marked
.B built\-in
or
.BR user ,
and the active default is flagged.
.SH OUTPUT AND NAMING
On the CLI, use
.B \-o
to choose the path explicitly. Over MCP, the
.B output_name
parameter is the preferred way to name a screenshot: pick a short, descriptive
slug such as
.I finding-01-sqli
or
.IR before-fix .
.PP
When no name is given, a fallback base name is generated as
.IR {working-dir}-{first-command-word} .
For example, running
.B cargo test
in
.I ~/Desktop/webapp
yields
.IR webapp-cargo.png .
Generated names are lowercased, runs of non\-alphanumeric characters collapse
to single hyphens, they are trimmed and capped at 60 characters, and a numeric
suffix
.RB ( \-2 ,
.BR \-3 ,
\&...) is appended to avoid overwriting an existing file.
.SH REDACTION
Redaction masks sensitive data in the rendered image so screenshots are safe to
share. The returned text keeps the original content unless
.B \-\-redact\-text
is given.
.PP
It is opt\-in: enable it per run with
.B \-\-redact
or
.BR "\-\-redact\-rules a,b" ,
or always\-on by setting
.B auto = true
in the
.B [redaction]
section of the config file.
.B [redaction] enabled
is the master switch: with
.B enabled = false
no rule ever runs and an explicit
.B \-\-redact
fails with an error instead of writing an unredacted image. The shipped default
is
.B enabled = true
with
.BR "auto = false" .
.SS Built-in rules
A set of rules is compiled in and enabled by default:
.BR ipv4 ,
.BR ipv6 ,
.BR mac ,
.BR aws_key ,
.BR aws_secret ,
.BR private_key ,
.BR jwt ,
.BR email ,
.BR hostname ,
.BR api_key ,
.BR github_token ,
.BR slack_token ,
.BR private_key_pem ,
.BR gcp_service_account ,
.BR azure_client_secret ,
.BR generic_api_key ,
.BR bearer_token ,
.BR connection_string ,
.BR discord_token ,
and
.BR hashicorp_vault_token .
Several provider\-token patterns are sourced from and inspired by Betterleaks
(MIT, https://github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks).
.PP
Matches are covered with a colored block and a short
.RB [ LABEL ]
tag. Rows joined by a soft line wrap are matched as one logical line, so a
secret that crosses the right margin is still masked. The rules favor precision
over recall, so ordinary output (source code, hashes, version strings, and
values such as
.I 127.0.0.1
or
.IR ::1 )
is left visible.
.SS Custom rules
Every
.IR .toml ,
.IR .yaml ,
and
.I .yml
file in
.I ~/.config/termshot/rules/
is loaded automatically; that directory is created on first run. Supply an
additional directory with
.BI \-\-rules\-path " DIR"
(or the
.B [redaction] rules_path
config key), whose rules are layered on top and win on name conflicts. TOML
files use the native
.B [[rules]]
format; YAML files use the Kingfisher rule format
.RB ( rules:
list with
.B name
/
.B id
and
.B pattern
/
.BR regex ).
Individual built\-ins can be overridden or disabled by name.
.SS Partial redaction
To reveal only part of a secret, either write a regex that matches just the
sensitive portion, or set
.B keep_prefix
and/or
.B keep_suffix
(character counts) on a rule or a
.B redact_screenshot
pattern. Those leave the first and last characters visible and mask only the
middle: for an AWS key
.IR AKIA... ,
.B keep_prefix: 4
shows
.I AKIA
followed by blocks.
.SS Agent workflow
The recommended flow for selective redaction over MCP:
.IP 1. 4
Capture with
.B execute_and_screenshot
(or
.BR render_ansi ).
The returned text keeps the original content even when the PNG is masked.
.IP 2. 4
Inspect the returned text and decide what else is sensitive.
.IP 3. 4
Call
.B redact_screenshot
with the returned screenshot path and a list of redactions, each either a regex
.B pattern
(with optional
.BR replacement ,
.BR keep_prefix ,
.BR keep_suffix )
or an explicit cell range
.RB ( row ,
.BR col_start ,
.BR col_end ).
The screenshot is re\-rendered in place from the in\-memory record.
.SS Labels and colors
Labels can be turned off with
.B show_labels: false
over MCP, leaving plain solid blocks. Block and label colors are configurable
engine\-wide via
.B [redaction] color
and
.BR "[redaction] label_color" ,
and per rule via a rule\(aqs
.B color
field (all as
.IR #RRGGBB ).
.SH THEMES
Built\-in themes are
.BR dark ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR catppuccin\-frappe ,
.BR catppuccin\-macchiato ,
.BR solarized\-dark ,
.BR solarized\-light ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox\-dark ,
and
.BR tokyo\-night .
They all use the bundled JetBrains Mono, and the shipped default is
.BR dark .
Run
.B termshot themes
to list every available theme.
.PP
User themes are loaded from
.IR ~/.config/termshot/themes/ ,
which is created empty on first run: each
.I .toml
file there defines one theme (foreground, background, and a 16\-color palette)
and may reference its own regular and bold fonts plus a
.B fallback_fonts
list of extra faces used for characters those fonts lack. Paths in all three
keys accept
.RB \(dq ~ \(dq
and resolve relative entries against the theme file\(aqs directory. A user
theme with the same name as a built\-in overrides it.
.SH VIEWPORT AND RETAINED OUTPUT
.B \-\-rows
and
.B \-\-cols
describe the terminal a command runs in: they decide where long lines soft wrap
and what a full\-screen program is told the window size is. They are not a limit
on what the screenshot shows.
.PP
Every line that scrolls out of that viewport is retained and rendered, so
.B termshot exec \-\-rows 10 \(aqseq 1 200\(aq
produces an image with all 200 lines, and the embedded
.B Description
metadata matches it. Use
.BI \-\-head\-lines " N"
or
.BI \-\-tail\-lines " N"
to render only one end; passing both is an error.
.PP
Retention is bounded by
.B max_scrollback_lines
in the config file (10000 lines by default, at least 1, capped at 60000), and
by a budget of 2000000 retained cells \- so a very wide terminal keeps fewer
lines than a narrow one. A command that overruns whichever limit applied prints
a warning naming it rather than silently dropping its oldest output.
.PP
.B \-\-head\-lines
is captured as those lines scroll past, not filtered out of what survived, so
it is the first N lines of the output even when the command printed a hundred
times more than the scrollback holds.
.B max_scrollback_lines
does not apply to it: that setting bounds how much of the
.I end
of a run is retained, while the head is streamed into a staging area bounded
only by the retained\-cell budget, so
.B \-\-head\-lines 10
returns lines 1\-10 at any configured capacity, down to 1.
.PP
Very tall captures also hit a rendering ceiling: 64 megapixels for the image and
320 MB of image buffers held at once, which window chrome with a drop shadow
reaches sooner because it needs two. Past it termshot fails with an error
pointing at
.B \-\-head\-lines
and
.BR \-\-tail\-lines .
.PP
Full\-screen (alternate\-screen) programs such as
.BR vim ,
.BR htop ,
and
.B less
repaint the whole viewport, so only their active screen is captured: the
scrollback from before they started is not part of what they are showing.
.B \-\-head\-lines
is the exception: output printed before such a program started is the head of
the run, so those lines are returned rather than the screen it painted. A prefix
shorter than the request falls back to the active screen.
.SH CONFIGURATION
On first run termshot bootstraps
.I ~/.config/termshot/
with a starter
.IR config.toml ,
a
.I themes/
directory, and a
.I rules/
directory. The config file
.RI ( ~/.config/termshot/config.toml
by default, or the path given to
.BR \-\-config )
controls the output directory, default font and font size, default terminal
size, how many scrolled\-off lines a capture retains
.RB ( max_scrollback_lines ),
shell, default theme, window chrome, and redaction behavior. A commented
example ships as
.I termshot.example.toml
in the source tree.
.PP
Several settings can also be overridden by environment variables:
.BR TERMSHOT_OUTPUT_DIR ,
.BR TERMSHOT_FONT_PATH ,
.BR TERMSHOT_FONT_SIZE ,
.BR TERMSHOT_COLS ,
.BR TERMSHOT_ROWS ,
.BR TERMSHOT_MAX_SCROLLBACK_LINES ,
.BR TERMSHOT_TIMEOUT ,
.BR TERMSHOT_SHELL ,
.BR TERMSHOT_THEME ,
and
.BR TERMSHOT_CHROME .
The pre\-rename
.B SCREENSHOT_MCP_*
spellings are still read, with a deprecation warning. The default output
directory is
.IR /tmp/termshot .
.SH EXAMPLES
Capture a themed test run with GNOME chrome for a blog post:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
termshot exec \-\-chrome gnome \-\-theme catppuccin\-mocha \-o post\-demo.png 'cargo test'
.EE
.RE
.PP
Produce a redacted, timestamped finding image for a pentest report:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
termshot exec \-\-redact \-\-timestamp \-\-chrome report \-o finding\-01.png 'nmap \-sV target'
.EE
.RE
.PP
Capture a long build but show only its last 20 lines:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
termshot exec \-\-tail\-lines 20 'cargo build 2>&1'
.EE
.RE
.PP
Render a previously captured log without executing anything:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
cmd \-\-color=always | termshot render \-
.EE
.RE
.PP
Combine before/after screenshots side by side for a pull\-request comparison:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
termshot compose \-\-layout horizontal \-o before\-after.png before.png after.png
.EE
.RE
.SH LIMITATIONS
Glyphs are rasterized from the configured font (the bundled JetBrains Mono
unless
.BR \-\-font ,
a theme, or
.B font_path
says otherwise), then from the bundled JetBrains Mono, then from the faces
listed in the theme\(aqs
.BR fallback_fonts ,
in that order. Box drawing, arrows, and common symbols emitted by tools such as
.BR bat (1)
or
.BR btop (1)
therefore render even under a font that lacks them. Scripts no font in the
chain covers, such as CJK and most Powerline or Nerd Font glyphs, are drawn as
.I .notdef
boxes until a covering face is added to
.B fallback_fonts
(see
.BR THEMES ).
.PP
Fallback faces must contain outline glyphs. Color\-bitmap emoji fonts such as
Noto Color Emoji and Apple Color Emoji are not supported; monochrome outline
emoji fonts may work.
.PP
termshot uses PTYs and POSIX signals: Linux and macOS are supported, Windows is
not.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/termshot/config.toml
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/termshot/themes/
User theme directory (one
.I .toml
per theme).
.TP
.I ~/.config/termshot/rules/
User redaction rule directory. Every
.IR .toml ,
.IR .yaml ,
and
.I .yml
file in it is loaded automatically.
.TP
.I /tmp/termshot/
Default output directory for generated PNGs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR nmap (1).
.PP
